How does blockchain technology work?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Blockchain technology is a decentralized method of recording transactions, using a distributed database to maintain a continuously growing list of records, called blocks. Each block contains a timestamp and a reference to the previous block, creating a chain of blocks, hence the term "blockchain." The information in each block is encrypted and shared across a network of computers, making it difficult to hack or alter the data without detection. <|endoftext|>
