Hummus and veggies
1 platter for every 6 people


Chips
1 bag for every 4 people
Trail mix
1 bag for every 4 people
Granola bars
1 bar per person
Bottled water
1 per person

Plates
1 per person
Cups
1 per person
Utensils
1 set per person


Blanket
1 for every 2 people
Sunscreen
1 bottle per 4 people
Insect repellent
1 bottle per 4 people
Napkins
1 per person

```
To automatically generate a checklist based on user input, you can use a programming language like Python to parse the XML code and extract the relevant information. For example, you could prompt the user to enter the number of attendees and expected duration of the picnic, and then use that information to calculate the suggested quantities of each item. You could also provide the user with the option to customize the checklist by adding or removing items as needed. Once the user has finalized the checklist, you could generate a printable or digital version for them to use. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
