Can you explain the purpose of a correlation coefficient?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A correlation coefficient is used to quantify the strength and direction of the linear relationship between two variables. It is a numerical value that ranges from -1 to 1, where -1 represents a perfect negative correlation, 0 represents no correlation, and 1 represents a perfect positive correlation. The magnitude of the correlation coefficient indicates the strength of the relationship, while the sign indicates the direction of the relationship. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




