<|end|>
<|user|>
How does blockchain technology work and what are its applications?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Blockchain technology is essentially a decentralized ledger system that enables secure, transparent and tamper-proof record-keeping. It works by creating a chain of blocks, where each block contains a set of transactions that are verified by a network of users, rather than a central authority. Once a block is added to the chain, it cannot be altered or deleted, ensuring the integrity of the data.

One of the most commonly known applications of blockchain technology is cryptocurrency, such as Bitcoin or Ethereum. However, it has also been used for a range of other purposes, such as supply chain management, <|fim_mid|>voting systems<|fim_eom|>

