How does climate change affect ocean currents?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Climate change can affect ocean currents by altering the temperature and salinity of the water. This can cause changes in the density of the water, which can in turn affect the movement of ocean currents. Rising sea levels caused by global warming can also affect ocean currents by changing the topography of the ocean floor. <|endoftext|>
