<|user|>
Can you explain how deep learning works?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Deep learning is a type of machine learning that involves the use of artificial neural networks with multiple layers of interconnected nodes, or "neurons." These networks are trained using large amounts of labeled data to learn complex patterns and relationships in the data, which can then be used to make predictions on new, unseen data. Deep learning has been particularly successful in areas such as image and speech recognition, natural language processing, and autonomous driving. The success of deep learning is due in part to the ability of these neural networks to automatically learn and extract features from raw input data, without requiring human intervention or feature engineering. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


