Additionally, because Sudoku puzzles are usually designed to be solvable using logic alone (i.e. without guessing), there are often multiple paths to the solution, each requiring different combinations of logical deductions. This makes the algorithm for solving a Sudoku puzzle more complex and nuanced than some other CSP-solving algorithms.

