Thank you for modifying the Swift code. Can you explain the time complexity of this algorithm?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n log n), where n is the number of words in the input array. This is because the algorithm first iterates through the input array to categorize the words and capture their frequency, which takes O(n) time. It then sorts the `frequency` dictionary using a sorting algorithm, which has a worst-case time complexity of O(n log n). Finally, it iterates through the `categories` and `frequency` dictionaries to print out the results, which takes O(n) time. Therefore, the overall time complexity of the algorithm is dominated by the sorting step, giving a total time complexity of O(n log n). <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


