<|asst|>
A computer mouse is an external device that is used to move the cursor on a computer screen. It typically has a scroll wheel, left and right click buttons, and a tracking sensor. On the other hand, a trackpad is a built-in input device on laptops or notebooks that allows users to move the cursor by sliding their fingers across the surface. While both devices serve the same purpose, some people prefer using a mouse for its ergonomic design and additional features. <|endoftext|>
