The third criterion for classification is based on whether the object is living or non-living. Apple, banana, and cow are living objects, while airplane is a non-living object.
4. Natural vs. Man-Made:
The fourth criterion for classification is based on whether the object is natural or man-made. Apple, banana, and cow are natural objects, while airplane is a man-made object.
