<|asst|>
A punchline is the concluding part of a joke that is designed to produce a strong emotional or humorous response from the audience. It typically comes at the end of a long set-up and provides a surprise twist that brings the joke together and makes it funny. The delivery of the punchline can make or break a comedian's act. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
