According to Smith (2019), "AI has the potential to revolutionize business processes" (p. 45).
In the above example, "Smith" is the author's last name, "2019" is the year of publication, and "p. 45" is the page number where the sentence can be found. 
In markdown, the citation would be formatted as follows: 
`According to Smith (2019), "AI has the potential to revolutionize business processes" (p. 45).`
And in APA format, the citation would be formatted as follows:
Smith, J. (2019). AI has the potential to revolutionize business processes. *Journal of Business Technology*, 45(2), 23-56. <|endoftext|>
