To sort the table in ascending order based on the appearance order column, follow these steps:
1. Click anywhere inside the table to select it.
2. Click on the "Data" tab on the ribbon at the top of the screen.
3. Click on the "Sort" button in the "Sort & Filter" section.
4. In the "Sort" dialog box, make sure that "Sort by" is set to "Appearance Order".
5. Make sure that "Sort On" is set to "Values".
6. Make sure that "Order" is set to "Smallest to Largest".
7. Click "OK" to sort the table.
Alternatively, you can use the following Excel formula to sort the table in ascending order based on the appearance order column:
`=SORT(A2:B5,2,TRUE)`
This formula sorts the range A2:B5 (which contains the table data) by the second column (which is the appearance order column) in ascending order. <|endoftext|>
