<|user|>
How can I retrieve the names and emails of all customers who made a purchase between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020 from the "sales" table in the database using a MATLAB function? Please provide the MATLAB function code to retrieve the data. The "sales" table has the following structure:
sales_id | customer_name | customer_email | purchase_date | purchase_amount
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 | John Smith | john@mail.com | 2020-02-15 | 100.00
2 | Jane Doe | jane@mail.com | 2020-11-20 | 75.00
3 | Bob Johnson | bob@mail.com | 2019-12-31 | 50.00
Make sure to only return customers who made purchases between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is the MATLAB function code to retrieve the names and emails of all customers who made a purchase between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020 from the "sales" table in the database:
```
function [customer_names, customer_emails] = retrieve_customer_info()
 % Connect to the database
 conn = database('database_name', 'username', 'password');
 
 % Construct the SQL query to retrieve the customer names and emails
 sql_query = "SELECT customer_name, customer_email FROM sales WHERE purchase_date >= '2020-01-01' AND purchase_date <= '2020-12-31'";
 
 % Execute the query and retrieve the data
 results = fetch(conn, sql_query);
 
 % Extract the customer names and emails from the results
 customer_names = results(:,1);
 customer_emails = results(:,2);
 
 % Close the database connection
 close(conn)
end
```
Replace "database_name", "username", and "password" with your database information. Call the function to retrieve the customer names and emails for all customers who made a purchase between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020. The function will return two arrays: customer_names and customer_emails. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That code you provided is helpful, but what if I want to retrieve the purchase amounts for each customer as well? Can you modify the SQL query in the MATLAB function to also return the purchase amounts for each customer who made a purchase between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Here is the modified SQL query in the MATLAB function that will retrieve the customer names, emails, and purchase amounts for all customers who made a purchase between January 1st, 2020 and December 31st, 2020:

```
SELECT customer_name, customer_email, purchase_amount 
FROM sales 
WHERE purchase_date >= '2020-01-01' AND purchase_date <= '2020-12-31'
```

This query will return three columns: customer_name, customer_email, and purchase_amount. Be sure to update the function accordingly to extract the purchase amounts from the results. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




