<|user|>
How can I create a Scala code that sends a formal email to my manager requesting for leave and adds a secret code that must be decrypted by the manager for the approval of the request? The secret code should be a combination of the current date and a randomly generated number. Also, please include the necessary code to set the subject, body, and recipient of the email.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To create a Scala code that sends a formal email with a secret code, you can use the JavaMail API. Here's an example code that you can modify to suit your needs:
```scala
import java.util.{Date, Properties}
import javax.mail.{Message, Session, Transport}
import javax.mail.internet.{InternetAddress, MimeMessage}
object EmailSender {
 def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {
 val recipient = "manager@example.com"
 val subject = "Request for Leave"
 val body = "Dear Manager,nnI would like to request for leave from [start date] to [end date]. Please let me know if there are any concerns.nnBest regards,n[Your Name]"
 // Generate secret code
 val dateFormat = new java.text.SimpleDateFormat("yyyyMMdd")
 val currentDate = dateFormat.format(new Date())
 val randomNum = scala.util.Random.nextInt(10000)
 val secretCode = s"$currentDate-$randomNum"
 // Set up mail properties
 val props = new Properties()
 props.put("mail.smtp.auth", "true")
 props.put("mail.smtp.starttls.enable", "true")
 props.put("mail.smtp.host", "smtp.gmail.com")
 props.put("mail.smtp.port", "587")
 // Set up mail session
 val session = Session.getInstance(props, new javax.mail.Authenticator() {
 override def getPasswordAuthentication(): javax.mail.PasswordAuthentication = {
 new javax.mail.PasswordAuthentication("your-email@example.com", "your-password")
 }
 })
 // Create message
 val message = new MimeMessage(session)
 message.setFrom(new InternetAddress("your-email@example.com"))
 message.setRecipients(Message.RecipientType.TO, InternetAddress.parse(recipient))
 message.setSubject(subject)
 message.setText(body + s"nnSecret code: $secretCode")
 // Send message
 Transport.send(message)
 println("Email sent successfully!")
 }
}
```
Make sure to replace "your-email@example.com" and "your-password" with your actual email address and password. Also, replace the placeholders in the "recipient", "subject", and "body" variables with your actual recipient's email address, subject, and message body.
Note that this code assumes that you're using a Gmail account to send the email. If you're using a different email provider, you may need to modify the mail properties accordingly. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between supervised learning and unsupervised learning in machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! In supervised learning, the algorithm learns from labeled data, where the correct output is already known. The goal of the algorithm is to learn a mapping between the input and output variables so that it can predict the output for new inputs. Examples of supervised learning include classification and regression.

On the other hand, in unsupervised learning, the algorithm learns from unlabeled data, where the correct output is not known. The goal of the algorithm is to discover patterns or structure in the data. Examples of unsupervised learning include clustering and dimensionality reduction.

In summary, <|fim_mid|>supervised learning involves learning from labeled data to make predictions<|fim_eom|>

