<|user|>
I'm trying to understand the concept of cognitive dissonance. Can you explain it to me and provide an example?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Cognitive dissonance occurs when a person holds two or more contradictory beliefs, attitudes, or values at the same time. This creates a feeling of discomfort or tension that motivates the person to reduce the inconsistency by changing their beliefs, attitudes, or behaviors. An example of cognitive dissonance could be a person who is environmentally conscious but drives a gas-guzzling car. To reduce the dissonance, they may rationalize their behavior by saying that they need the car for work or convince themselves that their other environmentally-friendly actions offset their car's impact on the environment. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


