Can you explain what irony is?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Irony is a literary technique where the intended meaning of a word or phrase is different from the actual meaning. There are several types of irony, such as verbal irony, situational irony, and dramatic irony. Verbal irony occurs when a speaker says something but means the opposite (e.g. saying "great weather" on a rainy day). Situational irony occurs when there is a contrast between what is expected to happen and what actually happens (e.g. a fire station burning down). Finally, dramatic irony occurs when the audience knows something that the characters do not (e.g. in Romeo and Juliet, the audience knows that Juliet is not really dead but Romeo does not). <|endoftext|>
