<|fim_suf|>, if we have a square-shaped object with a side length of 4 centimeters, the surface area would be:
4 cm x 4 cm x 4 = 16 cm²

As you can see, the surface area of a cube is greater than that of a square-shaped object with the same side length. This is because a cube has more faces than a square-shaped object which contributes to its larger surface area. <|endoftext|>
