<|user|>
Calculate the surface area of a square-shaped object with a length and width of 4 cm each.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The surface area of a square-shaped object is calculated by multiplying the length and width of one of its sides by 4. In this case, the length and width are both 4 cm each, so the surface area would be:
4 cm x 4 cm x 4 = 16 cm²
Therefore, the surface area of the square-shaped object is 16 square centimeters. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does the surface area of a cube compare to that of a square-shaped object with the same side length?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A cube and a square-shaped object with the same side length have different surface areas. The surface area of a cube is calculated by finding the area of each face and adding them all together. Since a cube has six faces, you would multiply the area of one face by 6. In contrast, the surface area of a square-shaped object is found by multiplying the length and width of one of its sides by 4.

For example, if we have a cube with a side length of 4 centimeters, the surface area would be:
<|fim_mid|>Area of one face = (4 cm) x (4 cm) = 16 cm²
Total surface area of cube = 6 x 16 cm² = 96 cm²

