<|user|>
How can I use C# to calculate the area of a triangle with vertices at the points (2, 0), (6, 4) and (3, 8)? Can you provide a code example?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Yes, here's an example C# code that calculates the area of a triangle with vertices at the points (2, 0), (6, 4), and (3, 8):
```
using System;
class Program
{
 static void Main(string[] args)
 {
 // Define the three points of the triangle
 double x1 = 2, y1 = 0;
 double x2 = 6, y2 = 4;
