What is the MATLAB code to plot a time series of the top three pressing issues related to climate change based on data from the Climate Change Knowledge Portal for the year 2019? 
Using the SQL database provided, the following query can retrieve the information:
SELECT indicator_name, value, year
FROM climate_change_data
WHERE country_code = 'WLD' AND year = 2019
ORDER BY value DESC
LIMIT 3;
Once you have the data, you can use the MATLAB code below to plot a time series of the top three issues:
data = [value1, value2, value3];
dates = datetime(year,1,1):calyears(1):datetime(year,1,1)+years(1)-calyears(1);
plot(dates,data);
xlabel('Year');
ylabel('Value');
title('Top Three Pressing Issues Related to Climate Change for the Year 2019');
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's the MATLAB code to plot a time series of the top three pressing issues related to climate change based on the query you provided:
```
% Connect to SQL database
conn = database('database_name', 'username', 'password');
% Execute query and retrieve data
query = 'SELECT indicator_name, value, year FROM climate_change_data WHERE country_code = ''WLD'' AND year = 2019 ORDER BY value DESC LIMIT 3;';
data = fetch(conn, query);
value1 = data{1,2};
value2 = data{2,2};
value3 = data{3,2};
year = data{1,3};
% Close database connection
close(conn);
% Create time series plot
data = [value1, value2, value3];
dates = datetime(year,1,1):calyears(1):datetime(year,1,1)+years(1)-calyears(1);
plot(dates,data);
xlabel('Year');
ylabel('Value');
title('Top Three Pressing Issues Related to Climate Change for the Year 2019');
```
Make sure to replace `database_name`, `username`, and `password` with the appropriate values for your SQL database. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
