Here is a code snippet for a program that can sort the list of animals based on their size and weight using the bubble sort algorithm:
```
animals = [('Elephant', 5443), ('Lion', 190), ('Rat', 0.22), ('Frog', 0.025)]
n = len(animals)
for i in range(n):
 for j in range(0, n-i-1):
 if animals[j][1] > animals[j+1][1]:
 animals[j], animals[j+1] = animals[j+1], animals[j]
print(animals)
```
This will output the sorted list of animals based on their weight:
<|fim_mid|>```
[('Frog', 0.025), ('Rat', 0.22), ('Lion', 190), ('Elephant', 5443)]
``` <|endoftext|>
