<|user|>
How is machine learning related to artificial intelligence?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Machine learning is a subset of artificial intelligence (AI) concerned with developing algorithms and statistical models that enable computer systems to learn from and make predictions or decisions based on data. In other words, AI provides the overarching framework for creating intelligent machines, while machine learning is one of the techniques used to teach those machines to perform specific tasks.

In practice, this means that machine learning algorithms are often used within larger AI systems to enable them to recognize patterns, learn from experience, and improve their performance over time. This is especially true for applications such as image recognition, natural language processing, and speech recognition, where large amounts of data can be used to train algorithms to recognize and respond to particular inputs. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


