Please write a function that finds the most repeated element in an array. The input array will have at least 10,000 elements and should be in the format of a [Java array]. Can you also modify the function to return all the elements that occur more than 50% of the time in the array? In this case, the elements returned should be sorted in descending order based on their frequency of occurrence.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here's a function in Java that finds the most repeated element in an array:
```java
public static int findMostRepeatedElement(int[] arr) {
 int n = arr.length;
 int maxCount = 0;
 int maxElement = arr[0];
 for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
 int count = 1;
 for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
 if (arr[i] == arr[j])
 count++;
 }
 if (count > maxCount) {
 maxCount = count;
 maxElement = arr[i];
 }
 }
 return maxElement;
}
```
