Here's a Java method that takes in a HotelStay object and returns a comment on the customer service based on the staff's friendliness and accommodation:
```
public String commentOnCustomerService(HotelStay stay) {
 String comment = "";
 int numStars = 0;
 if (stay.hasFreeBreakfast && stay.hasFreeWifi && stay.hasAirportShuttle) {
 numStars += 3;
 } else if (stay.hasFreeBreakfast || stay.hasFreeWifi || stay.hasAirportShuttle) {
 numStars += 2;
 } else {
 numStars += 1;
 }
 if (stay.hasPool && stay.hasGym && stay.hasSpa) {
 numStars += 3;
 } else if (stay.hasPool || stay.hasGym || stay.hasSpa) {
 numStars += 2;
 } else {
 numStars += 1;
 }
 if (stay.hasRestaurant && stay.hasBar && stay.hasLaundry) {
 numStars += 3;
 } else if (stay.hasRestaurant || stay.hasBar || stay.hasLaundry) {
 numStars += 2;
 } else {
 numStars += 1;
 }
 if (numStars >= 7) {
 comment = "The customer service was excellent! The staff was friendly and accommodating.";
 } else if (numStars >= 4) {
 comment = "The customer service was good. The staff was mostly friendly and accommodating.";
 } else {
 comment = "The customer service was poor. The staff was unfriendly and unaccommodating.";
 }
 return comment;
}
```
This method calculates a score based on the amenities provided by the hotel and then uses that score to determine the quality of the customer service. If the score is high, the method returns a positive comment on the customer service, while a low score results in a negative comment. <|endoftext|>
