<|user|>
Describe the concept of 'zero gravity'.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Zero gravity refers to the state of apparent weightlessness experienced by objects in orbit or free fall. It is often called microgravity or near-weightlessness, and it occurs when an object is in constant free fall around the Earth. In zero gravity, objects seem to float or drift, and they do not experience the gravitational pull that is normally exerted by the Earth. Instead, they are in a state of perpetual motion, orbiting the Earth at a constant speed, without any resistance from the atmosphere. The sensation of zero gravity is similar to that experienced in outer space or in parabolic flight, where the gravitational pull is significantly reduced or absent, making objects feel as if they are weightless. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some of the effects of zero gravity on human health?
