Of course! There are many different poetic forms that can be used to write about nature and the outdoors. One popular form is the haiku, which originated in Japan and typically consists of three lines with a syllable count of 5-7-5. Here's an example of a haiku about a sunset:
A golden sky fades
Birds chirp their goodnight songs
