In the same Java program, how can you modify the Group class to find the average price of items in a particular group?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To modify the Group class to find the average price of items in a particular group, you can add a method that calculates the average price of items in that group. Here's an example implementation:

```
public class Group {
 private String name;
 private List items;
 
 public Group(String name) {
 this.name = name;
 this.items = new ArrayList<>();
 }
 
 public void addItem(Item item) {
 this.items.add(item);
 }
 
 public double getAveragePrice() {
 double total = 0.0;
 for (Item item : this.items) {
 total += item.getPrice();
 }
 return total / this.items.size();
 }
 
 // getters and setters for name and items
}
```

You can then call the `getAveragePrice()` method on a particular group object to get the average price of items in that group. For example:

