What is the difference between an abstract class and an interface in C#?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Both abstract classes and interfaces are used to provide a blueprint for deriving new classes, but there are some key differences between them. An abstract class can have both abstract and non-abstract members, while an interface only has abstract members. A class can inherit from only one abstract class but can implement multiple interfaces. Additionally, an abstract class can have constructors, while an interface cannot. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
