If you encounter this issue on your computer, there are a few things you can do to try to resolve it. 
First, try restarting your computer. This can often resolve issues with software or hardware conflicts that may be causing the problem.
If that doesn't work, you can try running a virus scan to make sure your computer is free of malware or other malicious software that could be causing the issue.
If the problem persists, you may need to seek help from a professional computer technician or IT support specialist who can diagnose and fix the issue for you. <|endoftext|>
