<|user|>
What is dark matter and dark energy?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Dark matter is a hypothetical form of matter that is thought to make up approximately 85% of the matter in the universe. It does not emit, absorb, or reflect light, making it invisible to telescopes. Dark energy, on the other hand, is a mysterious form of energy that is thought to be responsible for the accelerating expansion of the universe. Its nature is not yet fully understood, but it is believed to make up approximately 68% of the energy in the universe. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain Einstein's theory of relativity?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Einstein's theory of relativity is a set of two theories: special relativity and general relativity. Special relativity explains how physical laws apply equally to all observers in uniform motion relative to one another, while general relativity explains how gravity works as a geometric property of space-time. These theories have been confirmed through numerous experiments and observations and have revolutionized our understanding of space, time, and gravity. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


