<|fim_suf|>, which are all served to the user as-is. Each page on the website is a separate HTML file, and they are all linked together using hyperlinks. A static website does not have an underlying database or any server-side scripting. Therefore, any changes made to the content of the website must be done manually by editing the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files.

On the other hand, a dynamic website uses server-side scripting to dynamically generate webpages in real-time. The content of a dynamic website is stored in a database, and whenever a user requests a page, the server retrieves the relevant data from the database and generates an HTML response on-the-fly. This allows for greater flexibility and interactivity since the website can change its content based on user input or other external factors.

To summarize, static websites are simple and easy to maintain, but lack the flexibility and interactivity of dynamic websites, which can adjust their content and functionality based on user input or external factors. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


