In the context of C# programming, can you please guide me through the process of extracting a specific set of words that are five characters long and relate to the concepts of deception and misleading? I was able to discover a table in Excel that contains some relevant terms, namely "Fraud", "Hoax", "Scam", "Cheat", and "Deceit". However, I'm unsure of the exact method to extract this data in C#. Could you kindly provide me with a sample code snippet that would allow me to retrieve the aforementioned words from the Excel table using multiple-step reasoning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that. Here's a sample C# code snippet that uses the EPPlus library to read an Excel table and extract the words that are five characters long and relate to deception and misleading:
```
using OfficeOpenXml;
using System.IO;
// Load the Excel file
FileInfo fileInfo = new FileInfo("path/to/excel/file.xlsx");
ExcelPackage excelPackage = new ExcelPackage(fileInfo);
// Get the worksheet and table
ExcelWorksheet worksheet = excelPackage.Workbook.Worksheets["Sheet1"];
ExcelTable table = worksheet.Tables["Table1"];
// Define the relevant keywords
string[] keywords = { "Fraud", "Hoax", "Scam", "Cheat", "Deceit" };
// Extract the relevant data
List relevantWords = new List();
foreach (ExcelRangeBase cell in table.Columns[1].Cells)
{
 string word = cell.Text.Trim();
 if (word.Length == 5 && keywords.Contains(word))
 {
 relevantWords.Add(word);
 }
}
// Print the relevant words
foreach (string word in relevantWords)
{
 Console.WriteLine(word);
}
```
In this code, we first load the Excel file using the EPPlus library. We then get the worksheet and table that contain the relevant data. We define the relevant keywords as an array of strings. We then iterate over each cell in the first column of the table, and check if the cell text is a five-letter word that is contained in the keywords array. If it is, <|fim_mid|>we add the word to a list of relevant words. Finally<|fim_eom|>

