<|user|>
In the given sentence "Every day is a new opportunity to learn and grow", please provide C# code to sort the words in descending order based on their length. Moreover, can you expand the code to also identify the word with the most vowels in the sentence and convert it to uppercase? Thank you!
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Here's the C# code to sort the words in descending order based on their length:
```
string sentence = "Every day is a new opportunity to learn and grow";
string[] words = sentence.Split(' ');
Array.Sort(words, (x, y) => y.Length.CompareTo(x.Length));
```
And here's the expanded code to identify the word with the most vowels and convert it to uppercase:
```
string sentence = "Every day is a new opportunity to learn and grow";
string[] words = sentence.Split(' ');
Array.Sort(words, (x, y) => y.Length.CompareTo(x.Length));
string mostVowelsWord = "";
int mostVowelsCount = 0;
foreach (string word in words)
{
 int vowelsCount = 0;
 foreach (char c in word)
 {
 if ("AEIOUaeiou".IndexOf(c) != -1)
 {
 vowelsCount++;
 }
 }
 if (vowelsCount > mostVowelsCount)
 {
 mostVowelsCount = vowelsCount;
 mostVowelsWord = word;
 }
}
if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(mostVowelsWord))
{
 mostVowelsWord = mostVowelsWord.ToUpper();
}
Console.WriteLine(string.Join(" ", words));
Console.WriteLine("Word with the most vowels: " + mostVowelsWord);
``` 
