Photosynthesis is the process by which plants convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. Chlorophyll in the plant's leaves absorbs light energy from the sun, and this energy is used to convert carbon dioxide from the air and water from the soil into glucose. Oxygen is also produced as a waste product. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
