Natural selection is the process by which certain traits become more or less common in a population over time, <|fim_suf|>, while individuals with less favorable traits are less likely to survive and pass on their genes. This leads to the evolution of species over time as beneficial traits become more common and less favorable traits become less common. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


