<|fim_suf|>, which involves the movement of the Earth's tectonic plates. When two plates collide, one plate may be forced underneath the other, causing it to melt and form magma. This magma then rises to the surface and cools, forming igneous rock. Over time, multiple layers of this rock can build up, creating a large mass of land known as a mountain range. Additionally, glaciers and erosion can shape and mold these mountains into their distinctive shapes. <|endoftext|>
