<|user|>
What kind of impact do mountains have on the climate and weather patterns?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Mountains play an important role in shaping the climate and weather patterns of the surrounding areas. The presence of a mountain range can cause air to rise and cool, leading to increased precipitation on the windward side of the mountain. This is known as orographic precipitation. On the leeward side of the mountain, however, the air descends and warms, causing drier conditions. Mountains can also act as barriers that affect the flow of air masses, influencing regional weather patterns. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
