<|end|>
<|user|>
How does the human brain process colors?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The human brain processes colors through a complex system of neurons and signals. The retina in the eye contains photoreceptor cells called cones that are sensitive to different wavelengths of light. These cones send signals to the brain, where they are processed in the visual cortex. The brain then interprets these signals as specific colors. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
