How can I use Python to transform the phrase "The cat meowed" into an italicized form in CSS, with the feline's vocalization denoted in a slanted font? Can you provide a sample code for this transformation? Also, please ensure that the font size of the slanted font is 2 points larger than the regular font size.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To transform the phrase "The cat meowed" into an italicized form with the feline's vocalization denoted in a slanted font in CSS, you can use the following code:
```html
The cat *meowed*
```
This code will create a paragraph with the phrase "The cat meowed" where the word "meowed" is italicized and has a font size 2 points larger than the rest of the text.
You can also use Python to generate this code dynamically. Here's an example:
```python
text = "The cat meowed"
slanted_word = "meowed"
font_size = 2
html = f"{text.replace(slanted_word, f'*{slanted_word}*')}

"
print(html)
```
This code will output the same HTML code as before, but you can customize the text, slanted word, and font size variables to generate different outputs. <|endoftext|>
