How does gradient descent work in machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Gradient descent is an optimization algorithm used to minimize the cost function in machine learning. It works by iteratively adjusting the model parameters in the direction of steepest descent of the cost function until it reaches a local minimum. The "gradient" refers to the derivative of the cost function with respect to the model parameters, which gives the direction and magnitude of the changes needed to reduce the cost. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
