<|asst|>
Sure! Kites stay aloft by using two basic principles of physics: lift and drag. The curved shape of the kite creates an area of low pressure above it, which generates lift and causes the kite to rise upwards. At the same time, the tail of the kite creates drag, which helps to stabilize its flight and prevent it from flipping over or spinning out of control. By controlling the amount of lift and drag generated by the kite, a skilled kite flyer can make it perform all sorts of impressive maneuvers in the air. <|endoftext|>
