<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between synchronous and asynchronous programming in JavaScript?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Synchronous programming means that code is executed in a sequence, one line at a time, and each line must finish executing before the next line can begin. Asynchronous programming allows multiple lines of code to be executed simultaneously, without waiting for each line to finish before moving on to the next. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
