<|user|>
How can I calculate the productivity of a research study using the term "prolific" in a scientific research paper? Can you provide an example using the following data set in MATLAB code:
prolific = [2 4 3 6 8 2 7 4 1 5];
total_words = [250 500 350 700 900 200 800 400 150 600];
I want to use the term "prolific" as a measure of productivity, where the higher the value, the more productive the study. How can I incorporate this into my analysis using MATLAB?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To calculate the productivity of a research study using the term "prolific" as a measure of productivity, you can calculate the ratio of the total number of words written to the number of prolific days. Here is an example MATLAB code that does this:
```matlab
prolific = [2 4 3 6 8 2 7 4 1 5];
total_words = [<|fim_suf|>];
% Calculate the productivity ratio
productivity_ratio = total_words ./ prolific;
% Find the average productivity ratio
average_productivity_ratio = mean(productivity_ratio);
% Display the average productivity ratio
disp("The average productivity ratio is " + average_productivity_ratio);
```
In this code, we first calculate the productivity ratio by dividing the total number of words by the number of prolific days. Then, we find the average productivity ratio by taking the mean of all the productivity ratios. Finally, we display the average productivity ratio. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
