<|end|>
<|asst|>
Object-oriented programming is a programming paradigm based on the concept of "objects", which can contain data and code that operates on that data. OOP aims to reduce complexity by breaking down a program into objects, which are essentially reusable software components with their own properties and methods. Objects can interact with each other through methods and inheritance, enabling software developers to structure code in a modular and organized way. OOP languages include Java, Python, <|fim_mid|>and C++. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
