<|user|>
Sure, here's the code:

```
import org.apache.spark.ml.clustering.KMeans
import org.apache.spark.sql.SparkSession

val spark = SparkSession.builder().appName("KMeansExample").getOrCreate()

// Load data
val dataset = spark.read.format("libsvm").load("sample_kmeans_data.txt")

// Trains a k-means model
val kmeans = new KMeans().setK(2).setSeed(1L)
val model = kmeans.fit(dataset)

// Evaluate clustering by computing Within Set Sum of Squared Errors.
val WSSSE = model.computeCost(dataset)
println(s"Within Set Sum of Squared Errors = $WSSSE")

// Shows the result.
println("Cluster Centers: ")
model.clusterCenters.foreach(println)
```
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Thanks for providing the code. To identify the cluster with the highest density and its corresponding centroid, we can modify the code as follows:

```import org.apache.spark.ml.clustering.KMeans
import org.apache.spark.sql.SparkSession
import org.apache.spark.ml.linalg.{Vector, Vectors}

val spark = SparkSession.builder().appName("KMeansExample").getOrCreate()

// Load data
val dataset = spark.read.format("libsvm").load("sample_kmeans_data.txt")

// Trains a k-mean model
val kmeans = new KMeans().setK(2).setSeed(1L)
val model = kmeans.fit(dataset)

// Obtain the cluster assignments for each data point
val predictions = model.transform(dataset)

// Compute the Euclidean distance between each data point and its assigned centroid
val distances = predictions.rdd.map(row => (row.getAs[Int]("prediction"), Vectors.sqdist(row.getAs[Vector]("features"), row.getAs[Vector]("centers")(row.getAs[Int]("prediction")))))

// Compute the number of points in each cluster
val countsByCluster = predictions.groupBy("prediction").count()

// Compute the density of each cluster
val densities = countsByCluster.join(distances).map{case (label, (count, distance)) => (label, count.toDouble / distance)}

// Find the cluster with the highest density
val maxDensityCluster = densities.reduce((a,b) => if(a._2 > b._2) a else b)._1

// Find the centroid of the cluster with the highest density
val maxDensityCentroid = model.clusterCenters(maxDensityCluster)

// Evaluate clustering by computing Within Set Sum of Squared Errors.
val WSSSE = model.computeCost(dataset)
println(s"Within Set Sum of Squared Errors = $WSSSE")

// Output the results
println(s"Cluster Centers: ")
model.clusterCenters.foreach(println)
println(s"The cluster with the highest density is cluster $maxDensityCluster with centroid $maxDensityCentroid")
```

This code adds some additional calculations to find the cluster with the highest density and its corresponding centroid. The output will include the cluster centers as well as information about the highest density cluster such as its label and centroid coordinates. Let me know if you have any other questions! <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




