What is the expanded version of the formula for finding the area of a triangle in a 2D plane given its three vertices as (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (x3, y3) in Markdown? Furthermore, include the additional constraints that each side of the triangle should be an integer, and the sum of the lengths of any two sides must be more than the remaining side. Could you also elaborate on how the vertices (3,4), (5,6), and (7,8) were selected to calculate the area of the triangle in the Markdown code block?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The expanded version of the formula for finding the area of a triangle in a 2D plane given its three vertices as (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (x3, y3) is:
```
Area = |(x1*(y2-y3) + x2*(y3-y1) + x3*(y1-y2))/2|
```
To ensure that each side of the triangle is an integer and the sum of the lengths of any two sides is more than the remaining side, we can use the following constraints:
- `abs(x1 - x2) + abs(y1 - y2) > abs(x1 - x3) + abs(y1 - y3) + abs(x2 - x3) + abs(y2 - y3)`
- `abs(x1 - x3) + abs(y1 - y3) > abs(x1 - x2) + abs(y1 - y2) + abs(x2 - x3) + abs(y2 - y3)`
- `abs(x2 - x3) + abs(y2 - y3) > abs(x1 - x2) + abs(y1 - y2) + abs(x1 - x3) + abs(y1 - y3)`
The vertices (3,4), (5,6), and (7,8) were selected arbitrarily to calculate the area of the triangle. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
