<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of time dilation in physics?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Time dilation is a phenomenon predicted by Einstein's theory of relativity. It states that time appears to move slower for objects that are moving at high speeds or in strong gravitational fields compared to objects that are stationary or in weaker gravitational fields. This effect has been observed in experiments involving atomic clocks on airplanes and satellites. The closer an object is to the speed of light, the more pronounced the effect of time dilation becomes. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
