<|user|>
What is the difference between machine learning and deep learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Machine learning (ML) is a subset of artificial intelligence (AI) that involves teaching machines to learn from data without being explicitly programmed. It is a method of training algorithms on a dataset to make predictions or decisions based on that data. Deep learning, on the other hand, is a type of machine learning that uses neural networks to analyze and interpret data. 

In deep learning, multiple layers of nodes in a neural network are used to identify patterns and relationships in large datasets. This allows for more complex and sophisticated data analysis than traditional machine learning techniques. Essentially, deep learning is a more advanced form of machine learning that requires a lot of computational power and large amounts of data to train the models effectively. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


