<|user|>
Suppose you have a table named "myTable" with the following data:
| ID | Name | Age | Score |
|------|--------|-------|--------|
| 1 | John | 25 | 80 |
| 2 | Mary | 30 | 90 |
| 3 | Jane | 28 | 70 |
| 4 | Tom | 32 | 85 |
What SQL query will give you the average score of all the entries in the "Score" column of the table "myTable"?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The SQL query to get the average score of all the entries in the "Score" column of the table "myTable" is:
```
SELECT AVG(Score) FROM myTable;
```
This will return the average score of all the entries in the "Score" column of the table "myTable". In this case, the result would be `81.25`. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some common data types in programming languages?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Some common data types in programming languages include integers (whole numbers), floating-point numbers (decimal numbers), strings (sequences of characters), booleans (true/false values), and arrays (collections of data). Other programming languages may have additional data types or variations on these basic types. For example, some languages have specific data types for dates and times, or for complex numbers. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


