<|user|>
How does temperature affect the rate of chemical reactions?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Temperature affects the rate of chemical reactions because it influences the kinetic energy of the reacting molecules. At higher temperatures, the molecules move faster and collide more frequently, leading to a greater likelihood of successful collisions and therefore a faster reaction rate. Conversely, at lower temperatures, the molecules move slower and collisions are less frequent, leading to a slower reaction rate. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
