<|user|>
How does deep learning differ from traditional machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Deep learning is a subset of machine learning that involves training neural networks with multiple layers to learn hierarchical representations of data. Traditional machine learning algorithms typically involve manually selecting relevant features and engineering them into the model. In contrast, deep learning models can automatically learn these features from raw data, making them more versatile and capable of handling complex tasks such as image or speech recognition. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some common techniques used in natural language processing (NLP)?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Some common techniques used in NLP include tokenization, stemming, part-of-speech tagging, named entity recognition, and sentiment analysis. Tokenization involves breaking up text into individual words or tokens, while stemming involves reducing these words to their root form to reduce redundancy. Part-of-speech tagging involves labeling each word with its grammatical role, while named entity recognition identifies and categorizes named entities such as people, places, and organizations. Sentiment analysis involves determining the overall emotional tone of a piece of text. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


