What is cognitive dissonance and how does it affect decision-making?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Cognitive dissonance is the mental discomfort experienced by a person who holds two or more contradictory beliefs or values at the same time, or who experiences a conflict between their beliefs and their actions. This discomfort can lead people to change their beliefs or behaviors in order to reduce the dissonance. In terms of decision-making, cognitive dissonance can lead people to make choices that are not in their best interests, as they may be more concerned with reducing the discomfort caused by conflicting beliefs or values than with making a rational decision based on evidence. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


