Planet Information
------------------
The planet you have landed on has a thin atmosphere and a rocky, desert-like landscape. Temperatures can vary greatly between day and night, so be sure to pack appropriate clothing.
Potential Dangers
-----------------
* Extreme temperatures
* Low oxygen levels
* Unstable rock formations
* Unknown wildlife
Map of the Planet
-----------------
![Map of the planet with key locations labeled](https://i.imgur.com/6fJy6jK.png)
Key locations include your landing site (marked with an "X"), a nearby cave system, and a mysterious structure in the distance.
Tips for Survival
-----------------
* Find a source of water as soon as possible, as it will be crucial for your survival.
* Look for edible plants and animals, but be cautious of any unknown species.
* Take breaks in shaded areas to avoid overheating.
* Stay in contact with your commander back on Earth for guidance and support.
Message from Commander
----------------------
"Congratulations on your successful landing, astronaut. Remember, your mission is to gather samples and data from the planet's surface. Stay focused and stay safe. We're all rooting for you back here on Earth." <|endoftext|>
