<|user|>
What is the difference between HTML and CSS?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language, which is used to structure content on a webpage. CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets, which is used to style and layout the content on a webpage. Basically, HTML defines what the content is while CSS defines how the content looks. HTML uses tags to define the structure of the content while CSS uses selectors to target specific elements and apply styles to them. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




