What is the difference between correlation and causation?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Correlation refers to the degree to which two variables are related to each other. Causation, on the other hand, refers to a relationship where one variable directly influences the other. A correlation does not necessarily imply causation, as there may be other factors that contribute to the relationship between the two variables. <|endoftext|>
