Here is a sample code in Ruby that generates a randomized haiku about summer:
```
# Define arrays of words for each line of the haiku
line1 = ["sunny", "hot", "bright", "shimmering", "scorching"]
line2 = ["beaches", "pools", "gardens", "fields", "forests"]
line3 = ["waves crash on the shore", "butterflies flutter by", "flowers bloom in fields", "trees sway in the breeze", "birds sing in the trees"]
# Shuffle the arrays to generate a randomized haiku
