<|user|>
What is the difference between artificial intelligence and machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Artificial intelligence (AI) is a broad field that encompasses any technology that mimics human intelligence. Machine learning is a subset of AI that relies on algorithms that can learn from data, rather than being explicitly programmed. In other words, machine learning is a way of achieving AI by training machines on large datasets, while AI includes other methods besides machine learning. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does neural machine translation work?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Neural machine translation is a type of machine translation that uses deep neural networks to translate text from one language to another. The system works by breaking down the source sentence into a series of vectors, which are then used to generate the target sentence. The neural network "learns" by adjusting the weights of its connections based on the quality of its output, improving over time as it is trained on more data. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


