Black holes form when massive stars run out of fuel and collapse in on themselves. The intense gravitational pull of the collapsed star is so strong that nothing, not even light, can escape it. This creates a region of space where gravity is so strong that it warps the fabric of space-time around it, creating what we call a black hole. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
