<|user|>
What is the Latex code to format a poem in the following structure?
begin{verse}
Line 1 
Line 2 
Line 3 
end{verse}
Also, how can I generate a Haiku poem using Java program from any given input poem while maintaining the Haiku format of 5-7-5 syllables? The input poem will be in the format mentioned above. Please provide the Java program code for the same.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To format a poem in the structure you mentioned, you can use the following Latex code:
begin{verse}
Line 1 
Line 2 
Line 3 
end{verse}
To generate a Haiku poem using Java program from a given input poem, you can follow these steps:
1. Split the input poem into individual lines.
2. For each line, count the number of syllables using a library like the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary.
3. Store the syllable count for each line in an array or list.
4. Iterate through the syllable count list and group lines together to form a Haiku (5-7-5 syllables).
5. Output the generated Haiku poem.
Here's an example Java program that implements the above steps:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Scanner;
public class HaikuGenerator {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
 // Read input poem
 System.out.println("Enter poem:");
 String poem = scanner.nextLine();
 // Split poem into lines
 String[] lines = poem.split(""); // Split by backslash
 // Count syllables for each line
 List syllableCounts = new ArrayList<>();
 for (String line : lines) {
 int syllables = countSyllables(line);
 syllableCounts.add(syllables);
 }
 // Generate Haiku
 List haiku = new ArrayList<>();
 int syllableCount = 0;
 for (int i = 0; i < syllableCounts.size(); i++) {
 int syllables = syllableCounts.get(i);
 if (syllableCount + syllables <= 5) {
 haiku.add(lines[i]);
 syllableCount += syllables;
 } else if (syllableCount + syllables <= 12) {
 haiku.add(lines[i]);
 syllableCount += syllables;
 if (syllableCount == 12) {
 break;
 }
 }
 }
 // Output Haiku
 if (haiku.size() == 3) {
 System.out.println(haiku.get(0));
 System.out.println(haiku.get(1));
 System.out.println(haiku.get(2));
 } else {
 System.out.println("Could not generate Haiku.");
 }
 }
 private static int countSyllables(String word) {
 // TODO: Implement syllable counting using CMU Pronouncing Dictionary
 return 0;
 }
}
```
Note that the `countSyllables` method is not implemented in this example. You can use a library like the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary to count syllables for each line. <|endoftext|>
