<|user|>
How does TEDx differ from TED Talks?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
While both TED Talks and TEDx events share a common goal of sharing innovative ideas, there are some differences between the two. TED Talks are curated by the main organization and feature well-known speakers on a range of topics. In contrast, TEDx events are independently organized and typically feature local speakers or community members, with the event's theme determined by the organizers. Additionally, TEDx talks are shorter in length than TED Talks and tend to focus on a specific topic related to the event's theme. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What are some notable TEDx talks that have gained widespread attention?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
