The effectiveness of the flu vaccine can vary from year to year depending on several factors. One important factor is how well the vaccine matches the circulating strains of the virus. Because the flu virus can mutate and change rapidly, <|fim_mid|>it is difficult to predict exactly which strains will be most prevalent in any given year. Scientists use a combination of epidemiological data<|fim_eom|>

