<|fim_suf|>, responsive, and interactive websites.

Back-end development, on the other hand, refers to the part of web development that deals with the behind-the-scenes functionality of web applications. This includes handling data storage, processing form submissions, managing user authentication and authorization, and communicating with external APIs. Back-end developers typically use server-side programming languages like PHP, Python, and Ruby to build the logic and functionality of web applications.

Overall, front-end and back-end development work together to deliver a seamless user experience and functional web application. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is responsive web design, and why is it important?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Responsive web design is an approach to web design that aims to create websites that adapt to various screen sizes and device types automatically. This means that the website will look and function optimally regardless of whether it is viewed on a desktop computer, tablet, or mobile device.

It is important because more people are accessing the internet using mobile devices than ever before. In fact, mobile web browsing has surpassed desktop browsing in terms of usage. By making sure your website is responsive, you can ensure that your visitors have a great user experience regardless of the device they are using. Additionally, responsive design can improve your website's search engine rankings since Google considers mobile-friendliness as a ranking factor. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


