<|user|>
How can I determine if a given string is a palindrome using C#? Can you provide an example using the string "madam"? 
Here is an example C# code to check if a given string is a palindrome:
using System;
public class PalindromeChecker {
 public static bool IsPalindrome(string str) {
 int i = 0, j = str.Length - 1;
 while (i < j) {
 if (str[i] != str[j])
 return false;
 i++;
 j--;
 }
 return true;
 }
}
To check if the string "madam" is a palindrome using this function, I would call:
bool isPalindrome = PalindromeChecker.IsPalindrome("madam");
This would return true, as "madam" reads the same way in reverse as it does forward.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
That is correct! The function checks if the first and last characters of the string are the same and continues to check the rest of the characters until the middle of the string is reached. If all characters match, then the string is a palindrome. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
