<|user|>
How can I determine if a given integer is a prime number in C#? Can you provide an example using the integer 17?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To determine if a given integer is a prime number in C#, you can write a function that checks if the number is divisible by any number other than 1 and itself. Here is an example code to check if the integer 17 is a prime number:

public static bool IsPrime(int num) {
 if (num < 2) {
 return false;
 }
 for (int i = 2; i <= Math.Sqrt(num); i++) {
 if (num % i == 0) {
 return false;
 }
 }
 return true;
}

bool isPrime = IsPrime(17);

This would return true, as 17 is a prime number since it is only divisible by 1 and itself. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
