<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of natural selection?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Natural selection is a process by which certain traits become more or less common in a population over time based on their ability to help individuals survive and reproduce. Essentially, organisms that are better adapted to their environment are more likely to survive and pass on their genes to future generations, while those that are less well adapted are less likely to do so. Over many generations, this can lead to the evolution of new species with unique characteristics and adaptations. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


