Herbivores are animals that primarily eat plant material, while carnivores are animals that primarily eat meat. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is the difference between a dolphin and a porpoise?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Although dolphins and porpoises may look similar, there are actually several key differences between the two. One of the main differences is their physical appearance, with porpoises having a more rounded head and shorter beak than dolphins. Additionally, dolphins tend to be more social and vocal than porpoises, and they also have a longer lifespan on average. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How do birds fly?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Birds are able to fly due to a combination of factors, including their lightweight bodies, powerful wings, and unique respiratory system. Unlike mammals, birds have air sacs that allow for unidirectional airflow through their lungs, which helps to supply oxygen to their muscles during flight. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
What is the process by which plants convert sunlight into energy?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The process by which plants convert sunlight into energy is called photosynthesis. During this process, light energy is used to split water molecules into hydrogen and oxygen, <|fim_mid|>with the resulting hydrogen being used to create energy-rich molecules such as ATP and NADPH. These molecules are then used to power the conversion of carbon dioxide into glucose<|fim_eom|>

