<|user|>
How do scientists determine the age of fossils?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Scientists use a variety of methods to determine the age of fossils, including radiometric dating, molecular clocks, and stratigraphic correlation. Radiometric dating measures the decay of radioactive isotopes to estimate when the fossil was last exposed to heat or sunlight. Molecular clocks compare DNA sequences between organisms to estimate how long ago they shared a common ancestor. Stratigraphic correlation uses the layers of sedimentary rock surrounding the fossil to establish its relative age within a specific time period. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


