<|user|>
That's great, but what if I want to add some padding to the text so that it doesn't touch the edges of the screen on smaller devices?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can add padding to the text by modifying the CSS code like this:
```
/* Base styles */
.big-text {
 font-weight: bold;
 font-size: 30pt;
 padding: 10px;
}
/* Hover effect */
.big-text:hover {
 color: red;
}
/* Responsive styles */
@media (max-width: 575px) {
 .big-text {
 font-size: 24pt;
 padding: 5px;
 }
}
@media (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 768px) {
 .big-text {
 font-size: 30pt;
 padding: 10px;
 }
}
@media (min-width: 769px) and (max-width: 992px) {
 .big-text {
 font-size: 36pt;
 padding: 15px;
 }
}
@media (min-width: 993px) and (max-width: 1200px) {
 .big-text {
 font-size: 42pt;
 padding: 20px;
 }
}
@media (min-width: 1201px) {
 .big-text {
 font-size: 48pt;
 padding: 25px;
 }
}
```
This will add 10 pixels of padding to the text by default, and adjust the padding for smaller screens according to the values in the table you provided earlier. This way, the text will have some breathing room on smaller screens and won't be too cramped against the edges. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


