Prime numbers are important because they can only be divided by 1 and themselves, which makes them unique. In this case, using a prime number ensures that the number of letters in the title and author's name combined cannot be evenly divided by any other number except 1 and itself. This means that the number is "special" in some way and adds an extra layer of significance to the books that meet this criteria. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
