<|fim_suf|>, long-duration activity that primarily relies on oxidative metabolism, which involves the breakdown of carbohydrates and fats in the presence of oxygen to produce ATP. This process is aerobic, meaning it requires oxygen, and can be sustained for longer periods of time. Bodybuilding typically involves performing multiple sets of exercises with moderate weights for several repetitions, with rest periods between sets.
