How can I utilize the Twit library and JavaScript to implement the Twitter API and compose a tweet discussing the latest advancements in artificial intelligence? Moreover, could you kindly provide a code snippet showing how to tailor the tweet with a custom message and hashtag? Additionally, it would be useful to incorporate guidelines on how to securely authenticate the API and manage any probable errors.
```javascript
const Twit = require('twit');
const config = require('./config'); // ensure this file contains the appropriate API keys and tokens
const T = new Twit(config);
const tweetMessage = 'Discussing the recent advancements in #AI. #ArtificialIntelligence #TechTrends';
T.post('statuses/update', { status: tweetMessage }, (err, data, response) => {
 if (err) {
 console.log(err);
 } else {
 console.log(`Tweeted: ${tweetMessage}`);
 }
});
```
For secure authentication of the API, make sure to generate and use unique access tokens and keys for your specific Twitter account. To handle errors, consider implementing try-catch blocks and handling specific error codes with relevant actions.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Great question! Here's a code snippet that shows how to use the Twit library and JavaScript to compose a tweet discussing the latest advancements in artificial intelligence, tailored with a custom message and hashtag:
```javascript
const Twit = require('twit');
const config = require('./config'); // ensure this file contains the appropriate API keys and tokens
const T = new Twit(config);
const customMessage = "Have you heard about the latest advancements in #AI? ";
const hashtag = "#ArtificialIntelligence #TechTrends";
const tweetMessage = customMessage + hashtag;
T.post('statuses/update', { status: tweetMessage }, (err, data, response) => {
 if (err) {
 console.log(err);
 } else {
 console.log(`Tweeted: ${tweetMessage}`);
 }
});
```
To securely authenticate the API, make sure to generate and use unique access tokens and keys for your specific Twitter account. You can do this by creating a Twitter Developer Account and generating your own API keys and tokens. 
To handle errors, consider implementing try-catch blocks and handling specific error codes with relevant actions. For example, if the error code is 187, it means that the tweet is a duplicate and has already been posted. In that case, you could log the error and move on to the next task. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
