<|end|>
<|asst|>
Both metaphors and similes are figures of speech that compare two things, but they differ in how they make the comparison. A metaphor compares two things directly by saying that one thing is another, while a simile compares two things using "like" or "as."

An example of a metaphor is "Life is a journey." This metaphor compares life to a journey, <|fim_mid|>suggesting that both have ups and downs<|fim_eom|>

