<|user|>
Can you explain the difference between inner join and outer join in SQL?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, an inner join returns only the matching rows in both tables being joined based on a specified condition, while an outer join returns all rows from one table and matching rows from the other table. There are three types of outer join: left outer join, right outer join, and full outer join. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
