How can we implement a Java function to calculate the total time length of all classes completed by a student in the Student category? The function should take the following parameters: the name of the sheet containing the class time length data, the time length data, the category data, the student name data, the respective category, and student name we want to calculate the total time length for. The function should use the formula =SUMIFS('Class Time Length'!B2:B100, 'Class Time Length'!A2:A100, "=Student", 'Class Time Length'!C2:C100, "=Student Name") to calculate the total time length.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here is an example Java function that should do what you're asking for:
```java
public double calculateTotalTimeLength(String sheetName, double[] timeLengthData, String[] categoryData, String[] studentNameData, String category, String studentName) {
 double totalTimeLength = 0.0;
 for (int i = 0; i < timeLengthData.length; i++) {
 if (categoryData[i].equals("Student") && studentNameData[i].equals(studentName)) {
 totalTimeLength += timeLengthData[i];
 }
 }
 return totalTimeLength;
}
```
This function takes in the name of the sheet containing the class time length data, an array of time length data, an array of category data, an array of student name data, the category we want to calculate the total time length for, and the student name we want to calculate the total time length for.
The function loops through the time length data and checks if the category and student name match the ones we're looking for. If they do, it adds the time length to the total time length.
Note that this function doesn't actually use the formula you provided, as that formula looks like it's meant to be used in a spreadsheet program like Microsoft Excel. Instead, this function performs the same calculation in Java code. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
