John has a bag of marbles. If he gives 1/4 of the marbles to his sister, he will have 45 marbles left. How many marbles did he have originally?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Let's assume that John had x marbles originally. If he gives 1/4 of the marbles to his sister, he will be left with 3/4 of the marbles, which is equal to 45 marbles.
Using this information, we can set up an equation: 3/4 * x = 45.
Solving for x, we get x = 60.
Therefore, John originally had 60 marbles. <|endoftext|>
