<|fim_suf|>, and static members are not inherited either (although they can be accessed using the superclass name).

In addition to inheriting members from the superclass, a subclass can also add its own members, such as additional instance variables or methods. It can also override methods from the superclass, which allows it to provide its own implementation for a method that was already defined in the superclass.

Overall, inheritance is a powerful tool for creating hierarchies of related classes, where each subclass adds its own unique behavior while still retaining the functionality of its superclass. <|endoftext|>
