 table {
 font-size: 12px;
 }
 }
 
Languages and Countries
=======================


| Language | Countries |
| --- | --- |
| English | [United States](#), [United Kingdom](#) |
| Spanish | [Spain](#), [Mexico](#) |
| French | [France](#), [Canada](#) |
| Chinese | [China](#), [Taiwan](#) |
| Arabic | [Egypt](#), [Saudi Arabia](#) |


```
3. The code above includes a basic HTML structure with a title and a table element. The table has two columns: Language and Countries. The table is styled using CSS to have a responsive design that works well on mobile devices.
4. You can customize the table by adding more languages and countries. Ensure that every country is linked to at least two languages to ensure sufficient representation.
5. Save the file with a .html extension and open it in a web browser to see the table in action.
