<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! The `@media` rule in the CSS code targets specific devices based on their screen size or orientation. In this case, the rule is targeting screens that are 600 pixels wide or less. This means that the styles within the `@media` rule will only be applied to devices with smaller screens, like mobile phones or small tablets.

The styles within the `@media` rule are modifying the `font-size` property of the table, making the font smaller so that it fits better on smaller screens. By using the `@media` rule, we can ensure that our HTML table looks good and functions properly on all types of devices, from large desktop screens to small mobile phones. <|endoftext|>
