<|fim_suf|>, while in a queue, the first element added is the first one to be removed (FIFO - First In First Out). 

For example, imagine you have a stack of books. You add three books to the stack, one at a time. The book you added last will be the first one you can take out of the stack. Alternatively, if you arrange the same books in a queue, the first book you added will be the first to come out.

Stacks and queues are used in many computer algorithms and data structures, such as compilers, operating systems, network protocols, and more. Implementations of stacks and queues can vary depending on the specific use case and programming language being used. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


