<|user|>
What is the difference between artificial intelligence and machine learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Artificial intelligence (AI) is a broader field that encompasses all aspects of creating machines that can perform tasks that typically require human-level intelligence, including but not limited to machine learning. Machine learning (ML), on the other hand, is a specific subset of AI that focuses on training machines to learn from data and improve over time. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of virtual memory in operating systems?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Virtual memory is a technique used by operating systems to allow a computer to use more memory than it physically has available. It essentially creates an illusion of having more memory than is actually present by temporarily transferring inactive data from RAM to disk storage. This allows programs to continue running even when they exceed the physical limitations of the computer's memory. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


