<|user|>
Can you explain how the HSL values are calculated from RGB values?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Certainly! Hue is calculated by first determining the maximum and minimum values of the red, green, and blue components. If the maximum and minimum values are the same, the hue is set to 0. Otherwise, the hue is calculated as follows: if red is the maximum component, the hue is set to (green - blue) / (max - min). If green is the maximum component, the hue is set to 2 + (blue - red) / (max - min). If blue is the maximum component, the hue is set to 4 + (red - green) / (max - min). Saturation is calculated by dividing the difference between the maximum and minimum component values by the maximum value. Lightness is calculated by taking the average of the maximum and minimum component values. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


