How can I arrange a list of natural beauty spots in alphabetical order using PHP code? 
Here is the current list:
$beauty_spots = array("Grand Canyon", "Yellowstone National Park", "Niagara Falls", "Yosemite National Park", "Glacier National Park");
I want to sort it alphabetically without using any built-in PHP sorting functions. How can I achieve this using a manual sorting approach? Please provide step-by-step instructions using systematic reasoning.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, I can help you with that! 
Here are the steps to manually sort the given list of natural beauty spots in alphabetical order using PHP:
Step 1: Create a loop that will iterate through each element of the array. We will use a for loop to accomplish this.
Step 2: Inside the loop, create another loop that will compare the current element with the next element in the array. We will use another for loop to accomplish this.
Step 3: If the current element is greater than the next element, swap their positions in the array.
Step 4: Continue this process until the outer loop has iterated through the entire array without making any swaps.
Step 5: Print out the sorted array.
Here's the PHP code that implements this algorithm:
```
$beauty_spots = array("Grand Canyon", "Yellowstone National Park", "Niagara Falls", "Yosemite National Park", "Glacier National Park");
$size = count($beauty_spots);
for ($i = 0; $i < $size; $i++) {
 for ($j = 0; $j < $size - 1; $j++) {
 if ($beauty_spots[$j] > $beauty_spots[$j+1]) {
 $temp = $beauty_spots[$j];
 $beauty_spots[$j] = $beauty_spots[$j+1];
 $beauty_spots[$j+1] = $temp;
 }
 }
}
foreach ($beauty_spots as $spot) {
 echo $spot . "  
";
}
```
This code will output the following sorted list:
```
Glacier National Park
Grand Canyon
Niagara Falls
Yellowstone National Park
Yosemite National Park
```
