<|user|>
Can you write a Scala code that returns the names of all bioluminescent jellyfish species?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here's a Scala code that returns the names of all bioluminescent jellyfish species:
```scala
import scala.io.Source
object BioluminescentJellyfish {
 def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {
 val source = Source.fromURL("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_bioluminescent_jellyfish")
 val html = source.mkString
 source.close()
 val pattern = """ *[(.*?)](/wiki/.*? ".*?")* |""".r
 val jellyfish = pattern.findAllMatchIn(html).map(_.group(1)).toList
 println(jellyfish)
 }
}
```
This code fetches the HTML content of the Wikipedia page listing bioluminescent jellyfish species, extracts the names of the species using a regular expression pattern, and prints them to the console. Note that this code requires an internet connection to fetch the page content. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How can we modify the Scala code to return only the names of bioluminescent jellyfish species that belong to the Pelagiidae family?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
We can modify the Scala code to return only the names of bioluminescent jellyfish species that belong to the Pelagiidae family by adding an additional filter statement to our existing code. Here's the modified code:
```scala
import scala.io.Source

object BioluminescentJellyfish {
 def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {
 val source = Source.fromURL("https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_bioluminescent_jellyfish")
 val html = source.mkString
 source.close()
 val pattern = """ *[(.*?)](/wiki/.*? ".*?")* |n [(.*?)](/wiki/.*? ".*?") |""".r
 val jellyfish = pattern.findAllMatchIn(html).toList.filter(x => x.group(2) == "Pelagiidae").map(_.group(1))
 println(jellyfish)
 }
}
```
We added a new regex pattern that matches the name of the family for each jellyfish species and used the `filter` method to select only the species that belong to the Pelagiidae family. Finally, we used `map` to extract only their names and print them to the console.

Note that this implementation assumes that the structure of the Wikipedia page remains the same, so it may not work if the page layout changes in the future. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




