What is the difference between a comet and an asteroid?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Comets are icy bodies that originate from the outer solar system, while asteroids are rocky or metallic bodies that originate from the inner solar system. Comets typically have highly elliptical orbits, and when they come close to the Sun, they can develop a coma, or a cloud of gas and dust around them, as well as a tail that points away from the Sun due to solar wind. Asteroids, on the other hand, typically have more circular orbits and do not develop comas or tails. <|endoftext|>
