const catJokes = [
 "Why don't cats play poker in the jungle? Too many cheetahs.",
 "Why did the cat join Instagram? To stalk meow celebrities.",
 "What do you call a cat who likes to eat beans? A purrito.",
 "Why do cats make terrible storytellers? They only have one tail.",
 "What do you call a cat that loves to bowl? An alley cat.",
 "Why don't cats like online shopping? They prefer a cat-alog.",
];
Can you write a function that will return a random cat joke from the array?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here's a JavaScript code that generates a random cat joke from the given array:
```
const catJokes = [
 "Why don't cats play poker in the jungle? Too many cheetahs.",
 "Why did the cat join Instagram? To stalk meow celebrities.",
 "What do you call a cat who likes to eat beans? A purrito.",
 "Why do cats make terrible storytellers? They only have one tail.",
 "What do you call a cat that loves to bowl? An alley cat.",
 "Why don't cats like online shopping? They prefer a cat-alog.",
];
function getRandomCatJoke() {
 const randomIndex = Math.floor(Math.random() * catJokes.length);
 return catJokes[randomIndex];
}
console.log(getRandomCatJoke());
```
The `getRandomCatJoke()` function uses `Math.random()` to generate a random index within the length of the `catJokes` array. It then returns the joke at that index. Finally, the `console.log()` statement calls the function and logs the random joke to the console. <|endoftext|>
