<|user|>
How can I modify this Go code to sort a slice of strings in reverse alphabetical order?
package main
import (
 "fmt"
 "sort"
)
func reverseSort(slice []string) {
 sort.Slice(slice, func(i, j int) bool { return slice[i] > slice[j] })
}
func main() {
 slice := []string{"banana", "apple", "orange", "grape", "kiwi"}
 reverseSort(slice)
 fmt.Println(slice)
}
I want to be able to input a slice of strings and have them sorted in reverse alphabetical order using a custom sorting algorithm. How can I modify this code to achieve that?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can modify the code by changing the sorting function to compare strings in reverse alphabetical order. Here's an updated code:
```
package main
import (
 "fmt"
 "sort"
)
func reverseSort(slice []string) {
 sort.Slice(slice, func(i, j int) bool { return slice[i] > slice[j] })
}
func main() {
 slice := []string{"banana", "apple", "orange", "grape", "kiwi"}
 reverseSort(slice)
 fmt.Println(slice)
}
```
The `reverseSort` function sorts the slice in reverse alphabetical order using the `sort.Slice` function and a custom sorting function that compares two strings and returns `true` if the first string is greater than the second string. This function is passed to `sort.Slice` as an argument. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does the `sort.Slice` function work in Go?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The `sort.Slice` function in Go sorts a slice using a custom sorting function that you provide. Here's the signature of the function:
```
func Slice(slice interface{}, less func(i, j int) bool)
```
The `slice` parameter is the slice you want to sort, and the `less` parameter is the comparison function that determines the order of the elements. The `less` function takes two indices and returns `true` if the element at the first index should come before the element at the second index in the sorted slice.

When you call `sort.Slice`, it sorts the slice in place using the `less` function you provided. It uses the quicksort algorithm to sort the slice with an average time complexity of O(n log n). <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




