<|user|>
Can you explain the concept of black holes?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Black holes are regions in space where gravity is so strong that nothing, not even light, can escape its pull. They form when massive stars collapse in on themselves at the end of their lives, creating a singularity – an infinitely dense and small point in space – surrounded by an event horizon beyond which nothing can pass. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
How does the universe expand?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The universe is expanding because it began with the Big Bang, a cosmic explosion that occurred about 13.8 billion years ago. Since then, <|fim_mid|>everything in the universe has been moving away from everything else<|fim_eom|>

