<|fim_suf|>, you would need a table that contains the continent information for each country. Assuming you have such a table named "Continents" with the following data:
Country | Continent
--------|----------
Brazil | South America
India | Asia
China | Asia
You can use the following SQL query to join the two tables and classify the countries according to their continent:
```
SELECT Countries.Country, Continents.Continent
FROM Countries
INNER JOIN Continents ON Countries.Country = Continents.Country;
```
This query will return a table with the following data:
Country | Continent
--------|----------
Brazil | South America
India | Asia
China | Asia
This shows that Brazil is in South America, while India and China are in Asia. <|endoftext|>
