What is the difference between a sonnet and a haiku?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A sonnet is a 14-line poem written in iambic pentameter with a specific rhyme scheme. It typically consists of three quatrains followed by a rhyming couplet. A haiku, on the other hand, is a three-line poem that originated in Japan. It follows a 5-7-5 syllable pattern and often focuses on nature or a particular moment. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
