<|user|>
How do vaccines work, and what is herd immunity?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Vaccines work by introducing a weakened or dead pathogen into the body, triggering an immune response and building up immunity without causing illness. Herd immunity occurs when enough people in a population are vaccinated or have natural immunity to a disease, making it difficult for the disease to spread and protecting those who are unable to receive vaccines or have weakened immune systems. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


