Dark matter is a hypothetical form of matter that does not interact with light or other forms of electromagnetic radiation, making it invisible to telescopes. Scientists believe that dark matter plays a crucial role in the structure and evolution of the universe, as it is thought to be responsible for the gravitational forces that hold galaxies together and account for the observed distortions in cosmic microwave background radiation. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
