<|user|>
How can I estimate the population of Fayetteville, AR and take into account the percentage of residents who commute to neighboring cities for work using JavaScript? Can you provide a code snippet to help me calculate this?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To estimate the population of Fayetteville, AR and take into account the percentage of residents who commute to neighboring cities for work, you can use the following formula:
Estimated population = (Actual population) / (1 - Percentage of residents who commute)
Here's a code snippet in JavaScript that calculates the estimated population:
```javascript
// Define the actual population and percentage of residents who commute
const actualPopulation = 87125;
const percentageCommute = 0.25;
// Calculate the estimated population
const estimatedPopulation = actualPopulation / (1 - percentageCommute);
// Print the estimated population
console.log(`The estimated population of Fayetteville, AR is ${estimatedPopulation.toFixed(0)}.`);
```
This code assumes that the actual population of Fayetteville, AR is 87,125 and that 25% of residents commute to neighboring cities for work. The `toFixed(0)` method is used to round the estimated population to the nearest whole number. You can adjust the values of `actualPopulation` and `percentageCommute` to match your specific scenario. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
