| 7 | India | 3,287,263 |
| 8 | Argentina | 2,780,400 |
| 9 | Kazakhstan | 2,724,900 |
| 10 | Algeria | 2,381,741 |
To calculate the percentage of the world's total land area occupied by the top 5 countries on this list, we need to add up the land areas of those countries and divide by the total land area of the world. 
The total land area of the world is approximately 148,940,000 square kilometers. 
The top 5 countries on this list (Russia, <|fim_suf|>, China, United States, and Brazil) have a total land area of 52,343,233 square kilometers.
So the percentage of the world's total land area occupied by these top 5 countries is:
