Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the code snippet provided, it seems that we need to fill in two missing functions to get the correct output. Here's the updated code with the functions filled in:
```
public class Main {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 int n = Integer.parseInt(args[0]);
 for(int i=1; i<=n; i++) {
 System.out.print(i*i + " ");
 }
 }
}
```
The first missing function is `Integer.parseInt(args[0])`, which will convert the first command line argument to an integer value and assign it to the variable `n`.
The second missing function is `System.out.print(i*i + " ")`, which will print out the square of each integer from 1 to `n` followed by a space. 
So, for example, if we run the program with the command `java Main 5`, the output will be:
```
1 4 9 16 25
```
