In the previous example I showed you, we used the DOM parser to parse the "currency.xml" file and retrieve the "Full Name" value for the currency used in Europe. We created a DocumentBuilderFactory object and a DocumentBuilder object, and then called the parse() method on the DocumentBuilder object to parse the XML file and create a Document object. We then traversed the DOM tree using the getElementsByTagName() method to find the "currency" elements and their "zone" attribute values. Once we found the element we were looking for, we used the getElementsByTagName() method again to find the "FullName" element and retrieve its text content.

