Sure! A cell array in MATLAB is a type of data structure that can hold elements of different types and sizes. Unlike regular arrays, which can only hold elements of a single type, cell arrays can hold any combination of numbers, strings, characters, and even other arrays or cell arrays. They are particularly useful for storing data that does not fit neatly into a rectangular grid, <|fim_mid|>such as lists of variable length or collections of heterogeneous objects. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
