<|end|>
<|asst|>
The speed of light and sound varies in different mediums. In general, light travels faster than sound in all mediums. In vacuum, the speed of light is approximately 299,792,458 meters per second, while the speed of sound is zero as sound cannot travel through vacuum. In air, the speed of light is still approximately 299,792,458 meters per second, while the speed of sound is around 343 meters per second. In water, the speed of light is approximately 225,000,000 meters per second, while the speed of sound is around 1,482 meters per second. In metal, the speed of light can vary depending on the type of metal, but it is generally slower than in vacuum, while the speed of sound is much faster than in air or water.
