<|user|>
What is the difference between a virtual machine and a container?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
A virtual machine is a software emulation of a physical computer that can run its own operating system and applications. In contrast, a container is an isolated environment that shares the host operating system with other containers, but has its own file system, resources, and settings. Containers are generally more lightweight and faster to start up than virtual machines. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>




