<|user|>
It's amazing to see how much the Olympics have grown and changed over the centuries. I'm curious - how are host cities chosen for the Olympics?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Host cities for the Olympic Games are chosen through a competitive bidding process. Interested cities submit formal bids to the International Olympic Committee (IOC), outlining their plans for hosting the Games, including proposed venues, transportation systems, and accommodations. The IOC then evaluates the bids based on a number of criteria, including the city's infrastructure, financial resources, and ability to host a large-scale event. After a thorough evaluation process, the IOC selects the winning bid and announces the host city for the upcoming Games several years in advance. <|endoftext|>
