Yes, can you explain the difference between a stack and a queue?
A stack is a data structure that follows the LIFO (last in, first out) principle, where elements are added and removed from the top of the stack. A queue, on the other hand, follows the FIFO (first in, first out) principle, where elements are added to the rear and removed from the front of the queue.
