"Enter if you dare, but first you must know,
The answer to this riddle, before you go.
I am not alive, but I grow;
I don't have lungs, but I need air;
I don't have a mouth, but water kills me.
What am I?"
The answer to the riddle is "fire." To open the gate, the person seeking entry would have to light a torch and hold it up to the stone arch. The heat from the flame would activate a hidden mechanism that would unlock the gate and allow entry.
This design would add an extra layer of security to the castle, as only those who know the answer to the riddle would be able to enter. It would also add a challenge for intruders, as they would have to figure out the riddle before they could gain access to the castle. <|endoftext|>
