Can you explain the difference between supervised and unsupervised machine learning algorithms?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Supervised machine learning algorithms involve training a model on a labeled dataset, where each data point has an associated label or output. The goal is to learn a function that can map inputs to outputs. In contrast, unsupervised machine learning algorithms do not have access to labeled data and instead find patterns or structure within the data without any explicit guidance. The goal of unsupervised learning is often to discover meaningful representations or groupings in the data. <|endoftext|>
